   59\t        before_selector = selector_region(child)\n    60\t        child.step(direction)\n    61\t        delta = frame_delta(before[:63], child.frame()[:63])\n    62\t        print(\n    63\t            \"ONE\", direction,\n    64\t            \"delta\", (delta[\"count\"], delta[\"bbox\"]),\n    65\t            \"selector_changed\", selector_region(child) != before_selector,\n    66\t            \"samples\", delta[\"samples\"][:16],\n    67\t        )\n    68\t        repeated = child.clone()\n    69\t        changes = []\n    70\t        previous = selector_region(repeated)\n    71\t        for turn in range(2, 10):\n    72\t            repeated.step(direction)\n    73\t            current = selector_region(repeated)\n    74\t            if current != previous:\n    75\t                changes.append(turn)\n    76\t                previous = current\n    77\t        print(\"REPEAT\", direction, changes)\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tA.run_program(\"dc22\", run)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"The ring probe reproduces a teleport hub rather than a conventional bridge: changing the selector makes an outward step from the hub land on isolated arms, and the patterned tile on the upper arm returns to the central network instead of completing the level. I’m switching to a macro-state search that preserves the full visible world and branches only on controls that actually change it; the preserved search omitted the hub’s right control, so I’ll first measure that baseline and then correct the action model."}}
